Subject: [PATCH] venus M2/M3: one NV12 frame to HEVC/H.264 on IRIS1 (vayu_venus=2)

Base: /mnt/ramdisk/merge-all (line vayu-test26 + wifi/cell merge; bsd/conf/files:167 and
hakios.input.c:346 already had M1, so those files are unchanged).  Patches the five files
below with -p1 at the tree root.
tools/venus-hfi/run.sh is a new file: chmod +x it (a plain diff carries no mode).

What it adds: the session wire format (SESSION_INIT/END, SET/GET_PROPERTY, SET_BUFFERS,
LOAD_RESOURCES, START, STOP, EMPTY/FILL_BUFFER, and the SESSION_INIT_DONE/PROPERTY_INFO/
compressed FILL_BUFFER_DONE/EMPTY_BUFFER_DONE/BUFFER_REQUIREMENTS parsers) to
bsd/sys/vayu_venus_hfi.h; the M2/M3 path to bsd/dev/vayu_venus.c (a buffer pool at IOVA
0x27e00000 in the same apps-SMMU context, SESSION_INIT domain ENC=1, HEVC 0x2000 or
H.264 0x2, the encoder's properties, the firmware's BUFFER_REQUIREMENTS, SET_BUFFERS,
LOAD_RESOURCES, START, FTB, ETB with a generated NV12 gradient, FILL_BUFFER_DONE with the
NAL list, the first 64 bytes in hex and /private/var/tmp/venus_out.h265); the boot-arg
documentation to bsd/sys/vayu_venus.h; and tools/venus-hfi from 84 to 161 host checks.

Everything stays behind vayu_venus=1|2, the HFI interrupt stays masked and polled, and
all evidence lines in the log are the ones the task's V1/V2 gates ask for.

